What is vendored
----------------
source/ holds upstream's files at the pinned commit, unmodified, limited to
what the build reads: CMakeLists.txt, cmake/, include/, src/, LICENSE,
examples/miniaudio.h, and ggml/ (its CMakeLists.txt, cmake/, include/ and
src/, keeping only the CPU and Metal backend folders). The other ggml backend
folders and upstream's tests, examples, bindings, scripts and documentation are
left out. source-manifest.json lists every file kept, with its size and
SHA-256, and every folder left out.

Four of upstream's own test files are vendored for Biorouter's offline tests.
No installer or package carries them.

  models/for-tests-ggml-base.en.bin, models/for-tests-ggml-tiny.bin
      Whisper's English and multilingual vocabularies and model settings, with
      no weights. Whisper is MIT licensed, Copyright (c) 2022 OpenAI.
  models/for-tests-silero-v6.2.0-ggml.bin
      The Silero VAD v6.2.0 voice detector in ggml form, byte identical to the
      detector Biorouter downloads on request. Silero VAD is MIT licensed,
      Copyright (c) 2020-present Silero Team.
  samples/jfk.wav
      Upstream's 11 second sample from John F. Kennedy's 1961 inaugural
      address.


